From: gtk-cross <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] build: skip icon cache generation when cross-compiling

adwaita-icon-theme's meson.build always finds gtk4-update-icon-cache and adds
an install script that runs it against the just-installed theme.  In a cross
build the target binary cannot run on the build machine:

  Running custom install script
    '/work/out/linux-aarch64/bin/gtk4-update-icon-cache -qtf ...'
  FAILED: ... could not be run.
  error: command failed (exit 127)

The cache is optional (GtkIconTheme scans the directory when it is absent),
and cross assets already skip the framework's post_install step.  Only register
the install script when not cross-compiling; native builds are unchanged.

This patch is applied only to the Linux-host cross targets.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -92,14 +92,16 @@
   endforeach
 endif
 
-gtk_update_icon_cache = find_program(
-  'gtk4-update-icon-cache',
-  'gtk-update-icon-cache',
-  required : true,
-)
-meson.add_install_script(
-  gtk_update_icon_cache,
-  '-qtf',
-  get_option('prefix') / adwaita_dir,
-  skip_if_destdir: true,
-)
+if not meson.is_cross_build()
+  gtk_update_icon_cache = find_program(
+    'gtk4-update-icon-cache',
+    'gtk-update-icon-cache',
+    required : true,
+  )
+  meson.add_install_script(
+    gtk_update_icon_cache,
+    '-qtf',
+    get_option('prefix') / adwaita_dir,
+    skip_if_destdir: true,
+  )
+endif
